# Full competency question (ADR 0048):
#   "What happened during this session, in what order, on which clock — and did
#    execution run to completion or stop early?"
#
# Improvement plan 2.3 question 2. Before ADR 0048 SSTIM could not answer any
# part of it: a session record said that it ran and for how long, and nothing
# more. That was the gap blocking an event-semantic projection such as HED,
# which describes occurrences.
#
# Why this is a Full question and not a smaller one: it joins the execution
# (Session), the controlled event vocabulary (Vocabulary), and the timing
# authority that makes the offsets mean something. Core describes a stimulus and
# has no execution at all; Core Plus adds calibrated magnitudes and still has
# no notion that anything occurred.
#
# The ordering comes from the offsets, never from statement order — an RDF graph
# is a set, so a consumer reading the timeline off the order triples happen to
# arrive in would get a different answer each time. Hence ORDER BY.
PREFIX sstim:   <https://w3id.org/sstim#>
PREFIX sstim-v: <https://w3id.org/sstim/vocab#>
PREFIX skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>

SELECT ?instance ?status ?authority ?origin ?offset ?event WHERE {
  ?instance a sstim:SessionInstance ;
      sstim:completionStatus ?status ;
      sstim:clockOriginSeconds ?origin ;
      sstim:hasTimingAuthority ?timingAuthority ;
      sstim:hasSessionEvent ?occurrence .
  ?occurrence sstim:sessionClockOffsetSeconds ?offset ;
      sstim:hasEventType ?eventType .
  ?eventType skos:prefLabel ?event .
  ?timingAuthority skos:prefLabel ?authority .
  FILTER(LANG(?event) = "en")
  FILTER(LANG(?authority) = "en")
}
ORDER BY ?offset
